1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:08,964
This is the Smart Attendance System, a B.E. project by team Innovative_Heads at VCET, Mumbai University.

2
00:00:09,214 --> 00:00:12,614
It takes classroom attendance using face recognition.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,695
Calling names takes several minutes of every lecture.

4
00:00:17,945 --> 00:00:20,705
Friends can answer for students who are not there.

5
00:00:20,955 --> 00:00:25,187
And a student can be marked present, then quietly leave a few minutes later.

6
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:32,745
A fingerprint sensor sits outside the classroom door, and every teacher scans a finger while entering.

7
00:00:32,995 --> 00:00:39,467
Inside, a camera on the wall faces the whole class, and a Raspberry Pi between them does the processing.

8
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:50,082
Each enrolled finger belongs to a subject, so the system knows which lecture has started, and the LCD greets the teacher.

9
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:58,584
During the lecture, the camera takes six photos of the class at random moments, so nobody can predict the next one.

10
00:00:58,834 --> 00:01:03,642
A student counts as present only if seen in at least 60 % of the photos.

11
00:01:03,892 --> 00:01:07,996
Someone who is marked at the start and then leaves ends up absent.

12
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:18,076
In each photo, faces are found with HOG detection and turned into 128 numbers.

13
00:01:18,326 --> 00:01:23,198
If those numbers are close enough to a known student, the photo counts for that student.

14
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:29,335
After every photo, the result is saved in MySQL.

15
00:01:29,585 --> 00:01:32,708
Meanwhile, the LCD counts down the lecture.

16
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:39,179
Students log in to see their attendance in every subject, lecture by lecture.

17
00:01:39,429 --> 00:01:45,560
The analytics page warns them early when their average falls below 75 % or 50 %.

18
00:01:48,067 --> 00:01:55,840
Faculty see the whole class, including who left early, correct a status or mark a leave, and download the record for Excel.

19
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:59,639
Students send leave applications, and teachers reply.

20
00:02:02,133 --> 00:02:07,325
The project won first place at the Oscillations technical paper presentation,

21
00:02:07,575 --> 00:02:13,428
and second prizes at Tech-A-Thon, the VNPS project showcase, and Electrowiz.

22
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:23,138
In future, every classroom can connect to one central server, saving time in every lecture across the college.

23
00:02:23,388 --> 00:02:30,585
Students could get an app and alerts for parents, and faculty automatic defaulter lists and timetable integration.

24
00:02:33,267 --> 00:02:38,374
Built by Mayank Patil, Omkar Joshi, Chandan Thakur and Parth Mhatre.

